(4)

“Notwithstanding the provisions of item 1.1, following foods are exempted from the requirement of the 
mandatory nutrition declaration:

•	
Unprocessed products that comprise a single ingredient including raw agricultural products 
such as wheat, rice, cereals pulses, fruits and vegetables or products that comprise a single 
ingredient;

•	
Bottled or packaged drinking water;

•	
A spice or mixtures thereof;

•	
Salt;

•	
Tabletop sweeteners;

• 
Coffee extracts, whole or milled coffee beans and whole or milled decaffeinated coffee beans, 
coffee, decaffeinated coffee, soluble coffee powder without any other ingredients;

• 
Tea including decaffeinated tea, instant or soluble tea or tea extract, decaffeinated instant or 
soluble tea or tea extract which do not contain other added ingredients than flavorings which do 
not modify the nutritional value of the tea;

• 
Natural vinegars and artificial vinegars without any other added ingredients;

•	
Flavorings;

•	
Food additives;

•	
Processing aids;

•	
Food enzymes;

•	
Gelatine;

•	
Yeast;

•	
Food in packaging or containers with a total surface area equivalent to or less than 100 cm2; and

•	
Food manufacturered by cottage industries.”;
